From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anxelok <anxelok@localhost>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 17:04:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stage cross-region entity moves and removals to the world
 owner under parallel entity ticking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When an entity moves across a chunk-section / region boundary or despawns
(death/discard) while being ticked in a parallel region bucket on a region
worker thread, Moonrise's per-region "off-main" thread check trips:
"Cannot move/remove entity off-main" (EntityLookup$EntityCallback.onMove /
onRemove), because moveEntity()/removeEntity() mutate shared per-world
entity-tracking tables that are only safe to touch on the world-owning
thread.

Mirror the existing entity-spawn staging (patch 0045): when staging is
active on a worker, defer onMove()/onRemove() into the per-dispatch
RegionTickStaging session and replay them on the world-owning thread in
RegionTickStaging.applyAndClear, after the parallel phase joins.

RegionTickStaging gains stageEntityMove()/stageEntityRemove() entry points
(returning false when not staging, so the serial/default path runs the
original onMove/onRemove inline, byte-identical to upstream). Moves are
coalesced per entity (one applyMove() reads the entity's final position) via
an insertion-ordered map keyed by the EntityCallback; removes are kept
ordered. applyAndClear applies, in strict order: events, writes, scheduled
ticks, MOVES, REMOVES, spawns — moves before removes so a remove never
unmaps an entity a later move still needs. A de-dup/staleness guard
(EntityCallback.isStale, true once the entity is unmapped from entityById)
skips a redundant second remove (an entity can be discarded twice in one
tick via checkDespawn + guardEntityTick) and any move of an already-removed
entity.

The EntityCallback onMove/onRemove bodies are factored verbatim into
package-visible applyMove()/applyRemove() so the replay re-invokes the
original Moonrise logic unchanged; EntityCallback is made public so
RegionTickStaging can hold it as a staged-op handle. moveEntity/removeEntity
internals are untouched. The multipart/boss owner-tick path (patch 0046)
stays as a belt-and-suspenders complement.


